      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyes flick to the side \u2014 a brief, deliberate glance toward the hunched figure at the next table.\n\n\"Toran,\" she says simply. \"He's the one who's kept the lock in working order these past years. The gate mechanism, the tumblers, the whole assembly \u2014 he's the only one who's touched it.\"\n\nToran Vex looks up sharply, caught off guard, his ink-stained fingers freezing mid-fidget. He swallows.\n\n\"I... I didn't design it,\" he says, voice thin and hurried. \"I just maintained what was already there. Oiling the pins, replacing a worn spring, checking for rust. The lock was already in place when I took the contract. I never asked who forged it.\"\n\nMara watches him for a beat, then turns back to you.\n\n\"Toran's been the gate's caretaker for about four years now. Before that? The lock was the domain of the Sable Quill \u2014 that's the courier who still lingers at the gate. She carried the original key, or so the story goes. But she's not exactly talkative these days.\"\n\nShe drums her fingers once on the table.\n\n\"Point is \u2014 if anyone knows the mechanical truth of that lock, it's Toran. And if anyone knows what happened *before* the sealing, it's the Quill.\""
    },
