      "narrative": "Your voice cuts through the rain, bouncing off the wet stone of the arch.\n\n\"Bram!\"\n\nThe name hangs in the air. Fades into the grey.\n\nNothing. No echo from the gate. No voice from the grass.\n\nThe Sable Quill watches you from under her hood. Her head tilts a fraction.\n\n\"He's not here,\" she says. No mockery in it. Just fact. \"He's been dead three days. They found him slumped against that crate I'm sitting on.\"\n\nShe pauses.\n\n\"You knew that already. Mara told you.\" A beat. \"So why are you calling for a dead man?\""
