      "narrative": "You drop to a crouch, scanning the wet earth beneath the arch. Rain pocks the mud. Pebbles, scattered and grey. A few crushed blades of grass. Nothing that suggests disturbed ground, nothing that hints at anything hidden or buried.\n\nYou run your fingers through the mud. Cold. Unremarkable.\n\nThe Sable Quill watches you work. When you straighten up, she's still staring.\n\n\"You expecting to find something under there?\" she asks. No edge to it \u2014 just curiosity. \"I sat on that crate for two days before anyone showed up. Didn't see Bram dig anything up. Didn't see him bury anything either.\"\n\nShe shifts her weight on the crate.\n\n\"He kept the key on him. Always. A heavy iron thing on a leather cord around his neck.\" She touches her own collarbone vaguely. \"It wasn't on him when they found him.\"\n\nShe lets that hang.\n\n\"So either someone took it off his body before the healer arrived, or...\" She shrugs. \"Or it's somewhere else.\""
