      "narrative": "The rain follows you all the way back. By the time you push open the Copper Finch's door, your cloak is heavy with it, dripping onto the scarred floorboards.\n\nThe warmth hits you first. Then the smell of woodsmoke and spilled ale. The murmur of voices that pauses, briefly, as heads turn to mark your entrance, then resumes.\n\nYour old table sits empty by the shuttered window. The same one you sat at before. The candle on it has burned low, wax pooling on the wood.\n\nAs you settle into the chair, the door to the back room swings open. Mara Venn emerges, a steaming cup in each hand. She crosses the room without hesitation and sets one down in front of you.\n\n\"Figured you'd be back.\" She takes the seat across from you, wrapping her fingers around her own cup. \"The gate doesn't give up its secrets easy, does it?\"\n\nShe takes a sip.\n\n\"Did the Sable Quill tell you anything useful, or did she just sit there being cryptic?\""
